  "description": "JAMPUM crystallizes in the monoclinic crystal system with space group P 21/n. Reported CIF formula moiety: C148 H192 Cl8 N32 O58 Tb8 Zn4 4+,2(Cl4 Zn1 2-). From the CIF bond table, Tb1 (Tb) has 7 O neighbors; Tb2 (Tb) has 7 O neighbors; Tb3 (Tb) has 7 O neighbors; Tb4 (Tb) has 7 O neighbors; Tb5 (Tb) has 8 O neighbors; Tb6 (Tb) has 8 O neighbors; Tb7 (Tb) has 8 O neighbors; Tb8 (Tb) has 8 O neighbors; Zn1 (Zn) has 1 O neighbors; Zn2 (Zn) has 1 O neighbors; Zn3 (Zn) has 1 O neighbors; Zn4 (Zn) has 1 O neighbors; Zn5 (Zn) has 0 O neighbors; Zn6 (Zn) has 0 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 4 pairs, 10 components; largest component is a chain with insufficient metal sites for a 3D shape classification. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.621-3.680 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 94.98-103.11°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula [Tb8Zn4L6Cl8(solvent)n][ZnCl4]2.",
